## Conversation
Fell out of the same working-tree audit as the rtk removal. Both keys had
been dropped by a Claude Code rewrite of settings.json. I restored them,
the user said remove them, so this commit makes the removal deliberate
rather than accidental.

## Actions
Deleted two keys from claude_settings.json via a Python json round-trip
(preserving key order with object_pairs_hook=OrderedDict) rather than a
text edit, so the result is guaranteed valid JSON.

## Errors & Mistakes
None in this commit.

## Dead Ends
Considered using `git add -p` to split claude_settings.json across the
three commits it participates in. Interactive git flags are unavailable in
this harness. Instead I reconstructed intermediate versions of the file
with Python, staged each, and committed -- effectively a manual hunk
split. That technique works well and is worth reusing.

## Hints for Future Agents
- install.sh line ~66 has a jq block that writes `.mcpServers` into
  ~/.claude.json. It does NOT reference marketplaces, so removing
  extraKnownMarketplaces here needed no install.sh change. The comment at
  install.sh:66 claiming "plugins configured via extraKnownMarketplaces in
  claude_settings.json" is now stale but was left alone.
- abatilo-core@abatilo-plugins resolves from the in-repo
  .claude-plugin/marketplace.json, not a remote marketplace. It is
  unaffected.

## Codebase Discoveries
~/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/ contains ~27 `temp_*` directories
alongside the real ones. Appears to be uncleaned scratch state from plugin
installs. Not touched, but it is noise if you go looking there.

